Build the OpenSSL backend against OpenSSL 4.

OpenSSL 4 makes ASN1_STRING opaque and returns const pointers from the
X509 name/extension getters. Read ASN1_STRING through its accessors
(ASN1_STRING_length/get0_data/type, all present since OpenSSL 1.1.0) and
cast the getters' results back in the q_ wrappers, so their declarations
and callers stay unchanged; the casts are no-ops on older OpenSSL.

